{# One card of the 4a/4b calendars. `card` is a row built by App\Service\ProgressionCalendarBuilder;
   `show_hours` adds the class badge + "08:00 – 10:00" line that only 4b carries (README §3: 4a
   cards are matière + séquence, "pas de sous-titre").

   `show_evaluation` - the colour AND the nature's name - is 4b only. On 4a a card stands for a whole
   SÉQUENCE, built by collapsing its séances into the first of them, so both were the FIRST séance's
   nature stated about the entire séquence: a séquence whose third séance carries the évaluation
   announced none, and one whose first does was announced as an evaluation throughout. On 4b a card
   is a single séance and the nature says exactly what it looks like it says, so it stays there.

   It hides the nature of the posed-evaluation cards too, whose nature is not subject to that
   artefact. That is deliberate rather than collateral: 4a is a ten-month overview built of one card
   per séquence, and the product owner's call is that evaluations are not what it is read for. The
   "Évaluations" filter above it still narrows the cards down; what goes is the per-card marking.

   `link_to_seance` (4b) points the title at the séance rather than the séquence. Three targets, in
   order of how much they actually say about the séance:

     1. the fiche séance, app_library_seances_show - the real one, phasing included;
     2. failing that, the séance's row on the fiche séquence, via its id="seance-<id>" anchor;
     3. failing that, the fiche séquence itself.

   Nothing falls through to no link at all while a séquence sheet is reachable. 4a always stops at
   the séquence: its card stands for the whole of it, not for any one séance. #}
{% set nature = show_evaluation|default(false) ? card.nature : null %}

{% set sheet_url = null %}
{% if link_to_seance|default(false) and card.seanceTemplateId and card.sequenceTemplateId %}
    {% set sheet_url = path('app_library_seances_show', {sequenceId: card.sequenceTemplateId, id: card.seanceTemplateId}) %}
{% elseif card.sheetReachable and card.sequenceInstanceId %}
    {% set sheet_url = path('app_program_sequences_show', {id: card.programId, sequenceInstanceId: card.sequenceInstanceId}) %}
    {% if link_to_seance|default(false) and card.seanceInstanceId %}
        {% set sheet_url = sheet_url ~ '#seance-' ~ card.seanceInstanceId %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}

<div class="cm-prog-card{{ nature ? ' cm-prog-card--' ~ nature.slug }}">
    {% if show_hours|default(false) %}
        <div class="cm-prog-card__head">
            <span class="cm-prog-card__badge"{% if card.cohortColor %} style="background: {{ card.cohortColor }}"{% endif %}>{{ card.cohortLabel }}</span>
            {% if card.start %}
                <span class="cm-prog-card__time">{{ card.start }}{% if card.end %} – {{ card.end }}{% endif %}</span>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="cm-prog-card__topic">
        {{ card.topicLabel }}
        {# 4b only: one card per créneau there, so naming the group is what tells the two cards of a
           séance reproduced per group apart. 4a collapses cards down to séquences, where the group
           has nothing to say. #}
        {% if show_group|default(false) and card.groupLabel %}
            <span class="cm-prog-card__group"{% if card.groupColor %} style="background: color-mix(in srgb, {{ card.groupColor }} 16%, transparent); color: {{ card.groupColor }};"{% endif %}>{{ card.groupLabel }}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if nature %} · {{ nature.labelKey|trans }}{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="cm-prog-card__title">
        {% if sheet_url %}
            <a href="{{ sheet_url }}" class="cm-prog-card__link">{{ card.title }}</a>
        {% else %}
            {{ card.title }}
        {% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if card.tooShort or card.needsReassociation %}
        {# §4.3 / §4.7 - both rules end in "signalée visuellement sur la vue de progression", which
           is this line. #}
        <div class="cm-prog-card__flag">
            {{ (card.needsReassociation ? 'progressionCardToReassociateFlag' : 'progressionCardTooShortFlag')|trans }}
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
